case('nonvacuous-negative-route','Owned negative routing controls','有归属的负路由对照','scripts/run-evals.js',315,345,
 'A negative routing example must route to its intended owner, not merely avoid one wrong skill.','Name the correct neighboring skill and require it to outrank the rejected candidate with nonzero match.','Test review-versus-test routing.','Pass write a regression test because the review skill scores zero, even though every skill scores zero.','Require test-driven-development to outrank code-review on write a regression test; fail the case if neither matches.','Negative precision cannot pass through an unmatched prompt.','This runner is a lexical approximation; actual host routing needs separate behavioral runs.','负路由例须转到正确归属，不只避开一个错技能。','命名正确相邻技能，并要求非零匹配且排序高于被拒候选。','测试评审与测试的路由。','写回归测试在评审得零分即通过，虽然全部技能零分。','要求测试技能在写回归测试上高于评审；两者均不匹配则失败。','负精度不靠无匹配提示空过。','此运行器仅词汇近似，实际宿主路由须另做行为运行。')
case('artifact-kind-grading','Grade the declared artifact kind','按声明的产物类型评分','scripts/run-evals.js',528,584,
 'Choose the grading evidence according to whether the promised artifact is execution or conversation.','Execution cases require real fixture work and tool traces; dialogue cases grade conversational turns only when that is the actual deliverable.','Evaluate a bug-fix skill and a requirements interview.','Grade both from the assistant final claim that it followed the process.','For the fix inspect failing-test/edit/run events; for the interview inspect its questions and wait behavior, without inventing a code-edit requirement.','A narrated implementation is distinguishable from performed work.','Artifact-kind exemptions must be reviewed; source dialogue cases that expect file installation can blur this distinction.','按承诺产物是执行还是对话选择证据。','执行例需真实夹具与工具轨迹；仅真正对话交付才按轮次评分。','评估修错技能与需求访谈。','两者都只看代理最终称遵守流程。','修错检查失败测试、编辑、运行事件；访谈看提问等待，不虚加代码编辑要求。','可区分叙述实施与实际工作。','类型豁免须复核；源中对话例若期望文件安装会模糊区别。')
case('grade-id-binding','Bind grader results to the full expectation set','评分结果绑定完整期望集','scripts/run-evals.js',429,473,
 'Validate grade identities and reconstruct totals from the declared expectation set.','Require one unique result per canonical expectation ID, retain canonical text and derive counts; reject missing/duplicate IDs or inconsistent integer summaries.','Grade five bug-fix expectations.','Accept a fluent report with four results and a summary claiming five passed.','Require IDs1–5 exactly once; compute passed/failed from their booleans; reject a missing result before reporting success.','Coverage and arithmetic cannot be invented by the grader summary.','Identity/schema checks do not establish the truth of the grader evidence or semantic judgment.','验证评分身份，按声明期望集重建总数。','每规范ID一个唯一结果，保留规范文字并派生计数，拒缺失重复ID或冲突整数摘要。','给五项修错期望评分。','接收四项流畅结果及称五项通过的摘要。','要求1至5各一次，按布尔结果算通过失败；报成功前拒缺项。','评分摘要不能编覆盖与算术。','身份模式检查不证明证据或语义判断真实。')
case('activation-not-outcome','Separate activation indicators from outcome scores','分开激活指示与结果评分','evals/README.md',43,61,
 'A skill firing is an activation observation, not itself proof of useful behavior.','Keep invocation indicator separate from substantive outcome graders and compare equivalent with/without-skill runs under pinned conditions.','Evaluate a review skill on a planted boundary bug.','Give success credit only because Skill was invoked.','Record invocation separately; score whether the boundary bug was found in both skill and baseline arms using the same case and rubric.','The measured difference concerns the delivered review rather than merely loading a skill.','Source reported run counts are attributed observations, not established efficacy; model/CLI/version changes confound comparison.','技能触发是激活观察，本身不证明有用行为。','调用指示与实质结果评分分开，固定条件比较有无技能的等价运行。','用植入边界缺陷评估评审技能。','只因调用Skill即给成功分。','调用单记，技能与基准两臂同用案例量规，评分是否发现边界缺陷。','测差关乎交付评审，不仅载入技能。','源运行次数是归属观察非确定效能；模型CLI版本变化干扰比较。',ids=[169])

